  "description": "<p>Washington State University is a public higher education institution in Pullman, Washington. The facility provides undergraduate, postgraduate and doctorate-level degrees in various fields.&nbsp;</p><p>Currently, Washington Stateâ€™s main campus is in Pullman, but the establishment has several further locations across the state. At these locations, the university supports over 20,000 students from various backgrounds. The institution also has a large international student community, with over 2,500 students from outside the US.</p><h2>What is the Washington State University acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The Washington State University acceptance rate is 86%.</p> <p>Across six different campuses, Washington State has a wide range of facilities for use in different degree programs. Among these facilities are libraries, research centres, digital classrooms and laboratories.</p><p>On the main campus in Pullman, Washington State has various state-of-the-art learning facilities.  In addition, the establishment has subject-specific facilities such as a veterinary and biomedical research building and the PACCAR Environmental Technology Building.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>Washington State has a vibrant and diverse community on campus. Students can find many extracurricular activities as well as welcoming and sociable campuses. Today students from all 50 states and over 100 countries attend the university.</p><p>Presently, the university has over 300 sports clubs and more than 70 intramural sports teams. Students can also join around 60 different faith and cultural clubs. Furthermore, the establishment encourages students to take up volunteering alongside their studies. As a result, 5,741 students were actively volunteering between 2019 and 2020.</p>",
