      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Washington State University is a public higher education institution in Pullman, Washington. The facility provides undergraduate, postgraduate and doctorate-level degrees in various fields.&nbsp;</p><p>Currently, Washington State's main campus is in Pullman, but the establishment has several further locations across the state. At these locations, the university supports over 20,000 students from various backgrounds. The institution also has a large international student community, with over 2,500 students from outside the US.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student Life",
      "value": "<p>Washington State has a vibrant and diverse community on campus. Students can find many extracurricular activities as well as welcoming and sociable campuses. Today students from all 50 states and over 100 countries attend the university.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>Today, students have a range of on-campus housing options at Washington State. The establishment has 13 different halls of residence. Also, students can choose from a variety of accommodation types whilst studying. These include single and double rooms, private housing and catering options.</p><p>However, around 25% of students live on campus, while the majority live in halls or shared or rented spaces in Pullman. The university offers support and guidance about living off campus and students can find rooms, apartments and other options through the support team.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sports",
      "value": "<p>Presently, the university has over 300 sports clubs and more than 70 intramural sports teams. Students can also join around 60 different faith and cultural clubs. Furthermore, the establishment encourages students to take up volunteering alongside their studies. As a result, 5,741 students were actively volunteering between 2019 and 2020.</p>",
      "image": null,
